==================================================
GLOBAL SDLC RULES
==================================================

PROJECT BOARD COLUMNS:
- Backlog
- Planning
- Ready
- In Progress
- Testing
- Review
- Done
- Blocked

BRANCH NAMING:
- feature/task-<id>-<slug>
- fix/task-<id>-<slug>
- hotfix/task-<id>-<slug>

PR NAMING:
- [TASK-001] Short Description

COMMIT FORMAT:
- feat(task-001): add authentication service
- fix(task-001): resolve token refresh issue
- refactor(task-001): simplify middleware

EVERY TASK MUST HAVE:
- Acceptance criteria
- Technical plan
- Linked PR
- Testing checklist
- CI/CD status
- Deployment notes (if relevant)

==================================================
WORKFLOW RULES
==================================================

PHASE 1 — PLANNING
==================================================

When user says:
- "create plan"
- "plan created"
- "create task"
- "breakdown issue"

You must:

1. Analyze the GitHub issue.
2. Generate:
   - Technical breakdown
   - Subtasks
   - Risks
   - Dependencies
   - Acceptance criteria
   - Testing strategy

3. Create/update GitHub tasks:
   - Create issues/sub-issues if needed
   - Link them properly
   - Add labels
   - Add estimates if supported

4. Register all tasks into the GitHub Project Board:
   - Move to "Ready"

5. Ensure issue contains:
   - Definition of Done
   - Task checklist
   - Related architecture notes

6. If GitHub automation can do this:
   - configure GitHub Actions / Project automation
   - prefer automation

Otherwise:
- execute using agents/tools.

==================================================
PHASE 2 — DEVELOPMENT START
==================================================

When user says:
- "start development task #001"
- "start task #001"

You must:

1. Move task to:
   - "In Progress"

2. Create branch:
   - feature/task-001-<slug>

3. Create DRAFT PR immediately.

4. PR requirements:
   - Link issue/task
   - Add initial implementation checklist
   - Add testing checklist
   - Add architecture notes if needed

5. Ensure:
   - all commits automatically attach to draft PR
   - PR references issue
   - issue references PR

6. Update project board automatically.

7. If no automation exists:
   - agent must execute GitHub API operations.

==================================================
PHASE 3 — DEVELOPMENT EXECUTION
==================================================

During development:

1. All commits must:
   - follow commit convention
   - belong to correct branch
   - appear in DRAFT PR

2. Agent responsibilities:
   - maintain clean commit history
   - detect missing tests
   - detect lint issues
   - detect architecture violations
   - warn if acceptance criteria are incomplete

3. Agent should continuously verify:
   - unit tests
   - lint
   - formatting
   - type checks
   - security checks

==================================================
PHASE 4 — DEVELOPMENT COMPLETE
==================================================

When:
- implementation finished
- unit tests pass

You must:

1. Move task:
   - "In Progress" → "Testing"

2. Convert PR:
   - DRAFT → READY FOR REVIEW

3. Update PR description:
   Include:
   - Summary
   - Changes made
   - Screenshots/logs if available
   - Risk analysis
   - Rollback strategy
   - Testing checklist

4. Create testing TODO checklist:
   Example:
   - [ ] Unit tests passed
   - [ ] Integration tests passed
   - [ ] Docker build passed
   - [ ] CI/CD passed
   - [ ] Security scan passed
   - [ ] Manual QA passed
   - [ ] Documentation updated

==================================================
PHASE 5 — TESTING & CI/CD
==================================================

When CI/CD pipelines execute:

Automatically monitor:
- GitHub Actions
- Docker build
- Integration tests
- E2E tests
- Security scans
- Deployment preview

If successful:
- mark corresponding checklist items complete

If failed:
1. Comment failure summary in PR
2. Move task:
   - Testing → Blocked (if severe)
3. Suggest fixes

==================================================
PHASE 6 — REVIEW & MERGE
==================================================

Before merge:
Ensure:
- all required checks passed
- approvals completed
- no unresolved comments
- testing checklist complete

After PR merged:

1. Move task:
   - Review/Testing → Done

2. Close linked issue automatically.

3. Update project metrics.

4. Generate deployment summary:
   - PR link
   - commit hash
   - release note summary

